{"id":2319,"date":"2020-12-11T10:32:13","date_gmt":"2020-12-11T17:32:13","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/boulderqa.com\/?p=2319"},"modified":"2020-12-11T10:32:16","modified_gmt":"2020-12-11T17:32:16","slug":"boulder-qas-2021-recommended-browser-device-list","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/boulderqa.com\/boulder-qas-2021-recommended-browser-device-list\/","title":{"rendered":"BOULDER QA\u2019S 2021 RECOMMENDED BROWSER \/ DEVICE LIST"},"content":{"rendered":"\n<h1 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><span class=\"has-inline-color has-content-secondary-color\">BOULDER QA\u2019S 2021 RECOMMENDED BROWSER \/ DEVICE LIST<\/span><\/h1>\n\n\n\n<p>Each year we send our partners recommendations for Browsers and Devices for the coming year based on Browser and Device statistics.\u00a0 If our partners do not have access to website or application usage analytics or defined browser\/device specifications, then they use this data when sizing new projects for development and QA.\u00a0 With 2021 nearly here we wanted to publish our recommendations to not just our partners, but to our readers as well.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>With technology constantly changing with new operating systems, faster hardware and better screen resolutions it is challenge for us as technologists and our business partners to keep up with the latest trends and new hardware on the scene. We regularly check statistics to make sure that we are reviewing sites and applications using the best information available.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>We also wanted to share what devices that we have physically in our QA Lab as well as how we address devices that we may not have physical devices for.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>What browsers and devices are we recommending for 2021 and how do we come up with the recommendations for the coming year? This post is broken down into 3 sections:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><li><a href=\"#2020-Recommended-Browser-Device-List\">2021 Recommended Browser \/ Device List<\/a><\/li><li><a href=\"#Usage-Statistics\">Usage Statistics<\/a><ul><li><a href=\"#Desktop-Browser-Market-Share\">Desktop Browser Market Share<\/a><\/li><li><a href=\"#iOS-Version-Market-Share\">iOS Version Market Share<\/a><\/li><li><a href=\"#Android-Version-Market-Share\">Android Version Market Share<\/a><\/li><\/ul><\/li><li>\u00a0<a href=\"#Boulder-QA-Test-Lab\">Boulder QA Test Lab<\/a><\/li><\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h1 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"2020-Recommended-Browser-Device-List\"><span class=\"has-inline-color has-content-secondary-color\">2021 Recommended Browser \/ Device List<\/span><\/h1>\n\n\n\n<p>The following outlines BQA\u2019s recommended Browser \/ Device List for 2021 based on the statistics we have obtained from Global Stats statcounter (<a rel=\"noreferrer noopener\" aria-label=\"https:\/\/gs.statcounter.com (opens in a new tab)\" href=\"https:\/\/gs.statcounter.com\" target=\"_blank\">https:\/\/gs.statcounter.com<\/a>).<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><span class=\"has-inline-color has-content-secondary-color\">Browsers<\/span><\/h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><li>Chrome: latest version available<\/li><li>Safari: latest version available<\/li><li>Firefox: latest version available<\/li><li>Edge (Chromium) on Windows 10<\/li><\/ul>\n\n\n\n<p><strong><span class=\"has-inline-color has-content-primary-color\">NOTE<\/span>: <\/strong>Microsoft End of life dates for IE11 and Edge Legacy are as follows:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><li>IE11: August 17, 2021<\/li><li>Edge Legacy: March 9, 2021&nbsp;<\/li><\/ul>\n\n\n\n<p><a href=\"https:\/\/docs.microsoft.com\/en-us\/lifecycle\/announcements\/m365-ie11-microsoft-edge-legacy\">https:\/\/docs.microsoft.com\/en-us\/lifecycle\/announcements\/m365-ie11-microsoft-edge-legacy<\/a><\/p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><span class=\"has-inline-color has-content-secondary-color\">Android Devices<\/span><\/h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><li>Samsung S10 \/ OS 10<\/li><li>Google Pixel 3 \/ OS 9<\/li><li>Google Pixel \/ OS 8 (As Required)<\/li><\/ul>\n\n\n\n<p><strong><span class=\"has-inline-color has-content-primary-color\">NOTE<\/span>: <\/strong>Android OS 11 has been released and is currently available on some Pixel devices.\u00a0 Samsung is expected to start releasing OS 11 to their devices by year end.\u00a0 We will keep an eye on the OS 11 market share, currently at 0.3% and once it exceeds 5% we will look at starting to include it into our test suite of devices.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><span class=\"has-inline-color has-content-secondary-color\">iOS Devices<\/span><\/h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><li>iPhone 12 \/ iOS 14<\/li><li>iPhone XS \/ IOS 13<\/li><li>iPhone 8 \/ iOS 14<\/li><li>iPhone Mini \/ iOS 14<\/li><li>iPad Pro 10.5 \/ iOS 14<\/li><\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h1 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"Usage-Statistics\"><span class=\"has-inline-color has-content-secondary-color\">Usage Statistics<\/span><\/h1>\n\n\n\n<p>Boulder QA has reviewed a number of sites that provide market share statistics across platforms and operating systems. We really like the flexibility of Global Stats statcounter (<a href=\"https:\/\/gs.statcounter.com\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">https:\/\/gs.statcounter.com<\/a>). Global Stats calculate their statistics on the basis of more than 10 billion page views per month by people from all over the world onto their 2 million+ member sites. Global Stats allows the user to review the market share on a worldwide basis or narrow it down to a specific market region, for example the United States<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>With a majority of the Boulder QA partners and users located in the United States we are able to view this specific region and provide a recommendation to our clients on which browsers and devices will provide them with the best coverage for the website or application. When we have a client outside of the United States, we can quickly adjust our inputs to their region and make recommendations with statistics to support their specific audience.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>The following are the statistics BQA used to support our recommendations for 2021.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"Desktop-Browser-Market-Share\">Desktop Browser Market Share&nbsp;<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p>United States for the Last 12 months (Oct 2019 \u2013 Nov 2020)<\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table><tbody><tr><td><strong>Chrome<\/strong><\/td><td><strong>Safari<\/strong><\/td><td><strong>Edge<\/strong><\/td><td><strong>Firefox<\/strong><\/td><td><strong>IE<\/strong><\/td><\/tr><tr><td>57.91%<\/td><td>18.44%<\/td><td>9.86%<\/td><td>6.64%<\/td><td>4.43%<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"576\" src=\"https:\/\/boulderqa.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/12\/StatCounter-browser-US-monthly-201911-202011-1024x576.png\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-2321\" srcset=\"https:\/\/boulderqa.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/12\/StatCounter-browser-US-monthly-201911-202011-1024x576.png 1024w, https:\/\/boulderqa.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/12\/StatCounter-browser-US-monthly-201911-202011-300x169.png 300w, https:\/\/boulderqa.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/12\/StatCounter-browser-US-monthly-201911-202011-768x432.png 768w, https:\/\/boulderqa.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/12\/StatCounter-browser-US-monthly-201911-202011.png 1280w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" \/><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<p>Source: <a href=\"https:\/\/gs.statcounter.com\/browser-market-share\/desktop\/united-states-of-america\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">StatCounter Global Stats &#8211; Browser Market Share<\/a><\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"iOS-Version-Market-Share\">iOS Version Market Share<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p>United States for the Last 12 months (Oct 2019 \u2013 Nov 2020)<\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table><tbody><tr><td><strong>iOS 14.1<\/strong><\/td><td><strong> iOS 14.2<\/strong><\/td><td><strong> iOS 13.7<\/strong><\/td><td><strong> iOS 14.0<\/strong><\/td><td><strong> iOS 13.6<\/strong><\/td><td><strong> iOS 12.4<\/strong><\/td><\/tr><tr><td>38.15%<\/td><td>20.27%<\/td><td>10.28%<\/td><td>8.82%<\/td><td>5.65%<\/td><td>4.73%<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"576\" src=\"https:\/\/boulderqa.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/12\/StatCounter-ios_version-US-monthly-201911-202011-1024x576.png\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-2322\" srcset=\"https:\/\/boulderqa.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/12\/StatCounter-ios_version-US-monthly-201911-202011-1024x576.png 1024w, https:\/\/boulderqa.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/12\/StatCounter-ios_version-US-monthly-201911-202011-300x169.png 300w, https:\/\/boulderqa.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/12\/StatCounter-ios_version-US-monthly-201911-202011-768x432.png 768w, https:\/\/boulderqa.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/12\/StatCounter-ios_version-US-monthly-201911-202011.png 1280w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" \/><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<p>Source: <a href=\"https:\/\/gs.statcounter.com\/ios-version-market-share\/mobile-tablet\/united-states-of-america\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">StatCounter Global Stats &#8211; iOS Version Market Share<\/a><\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"Android-Version-Market-Share\">Android Version Market Share<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p>United States for the Last 12 months (Oct 2019 \u2013 Nov 2020)<\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table><tbody><tr><td><strong>10.0 10<\/strong><\/td><td><strong>9.0 Pie<\/strong><\/td><td><strong>8.0 Oreo<\/strong><\/td><td><strong>8.1 Oreo<\/strong><\/td><td><strong><strong>7.0 Nougat<\/strong><\/strong><\/td><td><strong>5.1 Lollipop<\/strong><\/td><\/tr><tr><td>49.65%<\/td><td>23.73%<\/td><td>6.12%<\/td><td>5.94%<\/td><td>4.38%<\/td><td>2.96%<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"576\" src=\"https:\/\/boulderqa.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/12\/StatCounter-android_version-US-monthly-201911-202011-1024x576.png\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-2323\" srcset=\"https:\/\/boulderqa.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/12\/StatCounter-android_version-US-monthly-201911-202011-1024x576.png 1024w, https:\/\/boulderqa.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/12\/StatCounter-android_version-US-monthly-201911-202011-300x169.png 300w, https:\/\/boulderqa.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/12\/StatCounter-android_version-US-monthly-201911-202011-768x432.png 768w, https:\/\/boulderqa.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/12\/StatCounter-android_version-US-monthly-201911-202011.png 1280w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" \/><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group\"><div class=\"wp-block-group__inner-container is-layout-flow wp-block-group-is-layout-flow\"><\/div><\/div>\n\n\n\n<p>Source: <a href=\"https:\/\/gs.statcounter.com\/android-version-market-share\/mobile-tablet\/united-states-of-america\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">StatCounter Global Stats &#8211; Android Version Market Share<\/a><\/p>\n\n\n\n<h1 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"Boulder-QA-Test-Lab\"><span class=\"has-inline-color has-content-secondary-color\">Boulder QA Test Lab<\/span><\/h1>\n\n\n\n<p>The following is a list of physical devices that BQA currently has in their lab.&nbsp; We also use BrowserStack (<a href=\"https:\/\/www.browserstack.com\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">https:\/\/www.browserstack.com<\/a>) to supplement the physical devices that we have in inventory.&nbsp; BrowserStack provides BQA the ability to review websites on devices that we may not currently have in our Test Lab or if a client has a very specific device that they would like reviewed.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>While we believe the best review of any website or application is on a physical device, we have found that BrowserStack provides us the ability to expand our lab with confidence for specific client requests that may occur outside of physical devices that we currently have outside of our lab.&nbsp;&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>We have also used BrowserStack to help identify issues which may always be repeatable within our client\u2019s development environment. There have been cases where we have reported an issue to our development partners that they cannot reproduce in house. Using BrowserStack to verify the issue and allowing us to share those results with our development partners increases the ability to provide a quality product to the end users.&nbsp;&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Desktops<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><li>MacBook Pro<\/li><li>Windows 10 (Physical and Virtual Machines)<\/li><li>Windows 7 (Virtual Machines)<\/li><\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">iOS Devices<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><li>iPhone 12 Pro \/ iOS 14<\/li><li>iPhone 12 \/ iOS 14<\/li><li>iPhone 12 Mini \/ iOS 14<\/li><li>iPhone Xs \/ iOS 13<\/li><li>iPhone X \/ iOS 14<\/li><li>iPhone X \/ iOS 13<\/li><li>iPhone 8 \/ iOS 14<\/li><li>iPhone 7P \/ iOS 14<\/li><li>iPhone 7 \/ iOS 13<\/li><\/ul>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><li>iPad (2018) \/ iOS 14<\/li><li>iPad Pro 10.5 \/ iOS 14<\/li><li>iPad Mini 4 \/ iOS 14<\/li><\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Android Devices<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><li>Samsung S10 \/ OS 10<\/li><li>Pixel 3 \/ OS 9<\/li><li>Pixel \/ OS 8<\/li><\/ul>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><li>Samsung Galaxy Tab A \/ OS 8<\/li><li>Samsung Galaxy Tab E \/ OS 7<br><\/li><\/ul>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>BOULDER QA\u2019S 2021 RECOMMENDED BROWSER \/ DEVICE LIST Each year we send our partners recommendations for Browsers and Devices for the coming year based on Browser and Device statistics.\u00a0 If our partners do not have access to website or application usage analytics or defined browser\/device specifications, then they use this data when sizing new projects&#8230;<\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":1,"featured_media":0,"comment_status":"closed","ping_status":"closed","sticky":false,"template":"","format":"standard","meta":{"footnotes":""},"categories":[1],"tags":[39],"class_list":["post-2319","post","type-post","status-publish","format-standard","hentry","category-uncategorized","tag-browser"],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/boulderqa.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/2319","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/boulderqa.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/boulderqa.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/post"}],"author":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/boulderqa.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/users\/1"}],"replies":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/boulderqa.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/comments?post=2319"}],"version-history":[{"count":5,"href":"https:\/\/boulderqa.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/2319\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":2327,"href":"https:\/\/boulderqa.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/2319\/revisions\/2327"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"https:\/\/boulderqa.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=2319"}],"wp:term":[{"taxonomy":"category","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/boulderqa.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/categories?post=2319"},{"taxonomy":"post_tag","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/boulderqa.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/tags?post=2319"}],"curies":[{"name":"wp","href":"https:\/\/api.w.org\/{rel}","templated":true}]}}